-- Create the Bull Shoals tailwater river row, with real NHD geometry.
--
-- Generated by scripts/import-nhd-rivers-from-tnm.ts from USGS National Map
-- NHD HR HUC8 shapefiles (11010003 + 11010004 — the huc_cd carried by this
-- reach's own USGS sites), then committed here the way 00116 committed the
-- original seven: a DB rebuilt from migrations should not need to re-download
-- 38 MB of shapefiles to get the same line.
--
-- ── Why this river needed a trim, and every previous one did not ───────────
-- A natural river's extent IS its watershed, so the HUC set defines it. A dam
-- tailwater's extent is a management decision. NHD knows nothing about either
-- end of this one: "White River" runs continuously through Bull Shoals Lake
-- above and far past Guion below, and the untrimmed dissolve came out at
-- **260.6 miles** — starting up in the reservoir, ending well downstream of
-- anything AGFC manages. Both ends wrong, in the direction that makes a river
-- page claim water it does not describe.
--
-- Trimmed to 90.6 miles between:
--   Bull Shoals Dam        -92.574845, 36.3657191   (USACE, via the registry)
--   AR 58 bridge at Guion  -91.9479309, 35.9243379  (OSM; see below)
--
-- The generated endpoints land 38 m and 15 m from those points respectively,
-- which is NHD vertex spacing. The length corroborates independently: the
-- research puts Calico Rock at ~62 river miles and Sylamore at ~79, and Guion
-- is below both — 90.6 is where it should fall.
--
-- The downstream boundary is AGFC's, confirmed on their Bull Shoals Tailwater
-- page 2026-08-12: the Commission manages the fishery "from Bull Shoals Dam to
-- the Arkansas Highway 58 Bridge at Guion." The COORDINATE for that bridge is
-- OpenStreetMap's — a way tagged highway=secondary, ref="AR 58", bridge, 65 m
-- from the mapped river centerline, against 512 m and 4.5 km for the only
-- other AR 58 bridges in the search box. OSM is a map, not an agency: it is
-- good enough to cut a line at and is not a source for anything published.
--
-- Upstream boundary note: the FISHERY starts 100 yards below the dam (a
-- no-fishing zone), the WATER starts at the dam, and this is the water. The
-- regulation boundary is an overlay, not the river's extent.
--
-- active = false. Activation stays a human call after regime-aware validation
-- passes — and this river cannot show a condition badge at all until a local
-- rating exists that nobody has produced yet.


INSERT INTO rivers (name, slug, geom, length_miles, downstream_point, direction_verified,
  description, difficulty_rating, region, state, timezone, river_type, active)
SELECT 'White River (Bull Shoals Tailwater)', 'white-river-bull-shoals',
